What the AGPL means here
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

VisTest is network server software. Section 13 of the AGPL applies:

    If you modify VisTest and let anyone interact with it over a network --
    inside your company, as a hosted product, or as part of a larger platform --
    you must offer those users the complete corresponding source code of your
    modified version, under the AGPL, at no charge.

"Complete corresponding source" includes any code you link into the service:
your changes to the engine, your API additions, your frontend, and the scripts
used to build and install it.

Running unmodified VisTest for your own testing triggers no obligation. Neither
does keeping private modifications you never expose to anyone else over a
network.


